      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait what do you mean \"goblins of the airline world\"? i'm just trying to get home. also, how do i actually narrow down these options? some of these layovers look really short, like under an hour, is that actually doable or is it just a bad idea?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sorry about that, I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy. I just meant that some airlines are more agile and flexible than others, like a group of goblins darting through the underbrush, finding the best routes and deals.\n\nNow, let's get back to the task at hand. Navigating the options can be overwhelming, but think of it like a puzzle. You need to find the right pieces that fit together to create a cohesive solution. Here's a trick: focus on the total travel time, not just the individual legs of the flight. Look for flights that offer a shorter overall journey, even if the layovers are short.\n\nFor example, if you have a flight from LHR to HKG with a layover in Dubai, it might not be the best option if the layover is only 45 minutes. But if you have a flight from LHR to SIN with a layover in HKG, it might be a better option, even if the layover is only 1 hour.\n\nAnother thing to consider is the airline's reputation for reliability. Some airlines are like a group of goblins who are always getting into trouble, while others are like a group of goblins who are always working",
